  "description": "Ions from the source are accelerated by your electrode, then bent by the magnetic field of the large coil. In a uniform field the radius is r = √(2mT)/(qB), so the heavy ions (m = 4) land twice as far out as the light ones (m = 1). Ions leaving at slightly different angles re-converge after half a turn (180° focusing). One accelerating electrode must bring both masses, at both angles, to their detectors.",
